 Q4","e":"knx","d":"2026-01-21","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Andrew Hess","x":"Additionally, seasonal project activities in October had shorter duration than in the prior year, likely due to some freight having been moved earlier than normal given trade and tariff disruptions throughout 2025.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/22/knight-swift-knx-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"KNX 2025 Q4","e":"knx","d":"2026-01-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brad Stewart","x":"…its adjusted operating ratio 140 basis points year-over-year to 100.1%, driven by a 2.8% increase in revenue per load as well as structural cost reduction and improvement in network balance, which led to significant year-over-year reductions in empty repositioning, trade and chassis costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/22/knight-swift-knx-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"KNX 2025 Q4","e":"knx","d":"2026-01-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Andrew Hess","x":"So at the beginning of the year, we put initiatives in place to drive cost out of what we viewed as the biggest opportunity, 3 variable cost areas of maintenance, fuel and insurance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/22/knight-swift-knx-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"KNX 2026 Q1","e":"knx","d":"2026-04-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Miller","x":"Last year this time, we took a big step back when tariffs were announced as we pushed for improving our revenue per load, and that led to us losing some volume.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/knight-swift-knx-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"KNX 2026 Q1","e":"knx","d":"2026-04-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam Miller","x":"For reference, that is better than last year at this time when targeting slightly lower price increases often led to lower volumes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/2